  "about": [
    {
      "heading": "Start",
      "body": [
        "I studied industrial design, then switched to software. Standing between the two did me a lot of good: I get to turn thinking about form into code at the same time.",
        "These days I mostly work on interface design, design systems, and interactive experiments I build with Three.js."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The work",
      "body": [
        "I like carrying an idea from its first rough sketch all the way to a working interface on my own: the idea, the design, the prototype, and finally the real code.",
        "I like thinking of everything I write as a box — simple, tidy, and easy to build on top of."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Off the clock",
      "body": [
        "I play around with type, collect old game cartridges, and write small programs for no reason at all."
      ]
    }
  ],
